                        "glosses": [
                            "A female given name originating as a coinage."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "79565fea-46f6-4490-8f19-37a1d237c86c",
                                "sense_id": "b49d6992-0cd9-3575-936f-0768b482692d",
                                "text": "They lived about thirty miles from the Squire; and she told me, that I might be sure to find her out by one circumstance; for that they had a daughter with a very strange name, Pamĕla, or Pamēla; some pronounced it one way, and some the other."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "afc6a3d3-4da7-44b4-bdb4-a27370dad2b4",
                                "sense_id": "b49d6992-0cd9-3575-936f-0768b482692d",
                                "text": "- But, Pamela, did you say? - A queer sort of name! - I've heard of it somewhere! - Is it a Christian or a Pagan name? - Linsey-woolsey - half one, half t'other - like thy girl - Ha, ha, ha.'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef2f00ee-0391-4c52-b5c9-91f22f8ac02e",
                                "sense_id": "b49d6992-0cd9-3575-936f-0768b482692d",
                                "text": "\"It's almost too realistic, too digital and computery,\" complains Alexis Vogel, a veteran celebrity makeup artist who recently worked on \"Stacked,\" a high-def show starring Pamela Anderson."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
